UID:event-echoes-of-the-familiar@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T112054Z
DTSTART:20260710T060000Z
DTEND:20260930T200000Z
SUMMARY:Echoes of the Familiar
DESCRIPTION:Echoes of the Familiar exhibition explores the concept that home transcends mere physical space\, embodying a tapestry of memories intricately woven into its very walls. It is within these confines that the echoes of laughter from childhood games intermingle with the remnants of disagreements and tears shed upon pillows. Each drawer brims with knick-knacks whose purposes remain elusive yet evoke nostalgia. The scent of maternal cooking and the rhythmic snoring of a father create a comforting ambiance\, while the presence of a grandmother before the television grounds us in familial continuity. These shared experiences resonate universally\, forging a collective nostalgia for "al zaman al Jameel
LOCATION:Ithra - Museum - Gallery 2
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-echoes-of-the-familiar.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-tafasahu-make-room@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T112054Z
DTSTART:20260710T060000Z
DTEND:20270320T190000Z
SUMMARY:Tafasahu: Make Room
DESCRIPTION:Tafasahu: Make Room is an exhibition that showcases a commissioned installation by Saudi architect and artist\, Nada AlMulla\, which invites you to enter as a guest&mdash\;to pause\, gather and reflect on the conditions of belonging within the context of the traditional Majlis\, Arabic for "gathering space." Beyond being a place to receive and host guests\, the Majlis has been a vessel for the transmission of knowledge and heritage. The installation deconstructs this space into its essential elements while centering stories\, memories and subtle traces of everyday life that animated it: conversations shared over coffee\, the lingering scent of incense\, the rhythms of gathering and departure. Hospita
LOCATION:Ithra - Museum - Gallery 0
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-tafasahu-make-room.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-beaded-plant-suncatcher@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T112054Z
DTSTART:20260710T093000Z
DTEND:20260711T113000Z
SUMMARY:Beaded plant Suncatcher
DESCRIPTION:Sunlight has a way of bringing a space to life. As it passes through a window\, it fills a room with color\, movement\, and small moments that make a house feel like home. In this workshop\, participants create beaded plant sun catchers inspired by the light that streams through our windows and the natural elements we welcome into our homes. By combining colorful beads and delicate forms\, each piece is designed to catch and reflect sunlight\, creating shifting patterns of color and light. The result is a decorative artwork that celebrates the warmth of home through nature\, color\, and light.
LOCATION:Ithra - Ithra Tower - Level 9\, Room 2
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-beaded-plant-suncatcher.html
END:VEVENT
